:: Statement-only formalization of Logipedia corpus artifact fact.eq_fact
:: (logipedia__mizar__fact.eq_fact), catalog title "fact.eq_fact": for every
:: natural number, factorial is Leibniz-equal to the natural-type filter of
:: its factorial body. This file contains no proof.

environ
  vocabularies NUMBERS, NAT_1, FINSEQ_1, FINSEQ_2, RELAT_1, FUNCT_1,
    XBOOLE_0, SUBSET_1, TARSKI, CARD_1, XCMPLX_0, XREAL_0, XXREAL_0,
    ORDINAL1, NEWTON, REALSET1, INT_1, INT_2, ARYTM_1, ARYTM_3,
    CARD_3, VALUED_0, VALUED_1, WAYBEL_4, CARDFIL2;
  notations TARSKI, XBOOLE_0, SUBSET_1, ORDINAL1, CARD_1, NUMBERS,
    XCMPLX_0, XREAL_0, XXREAL_0, INT_1, INT_2, NEWTON, RELAT_1,
    FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2, FINSEQ_1, RVSUM_1, FINSEQ_2, NAT_1, NAT_D;
  constructors REAL_1, NAT_D, NEWTON, RELSET_1, FUNCT_2, NUMBERS,
    RVSUM_1, FINSEQOP, INT_2, WSIERP_1;
  registrations XBOOLE_0, RELAT_1, FUNCT_1, FUNCT_2, ORDINAL1, NUMBERS,
    XCMPLX_0, XXREAL_0, XREAL_0, NAT_1, INT_1, FINSEQ_1, FINSEQ_2,
    RVSUM_1, NEWTON, WSIERP_1, VALUED_0, VALUED_1, CARD_1;
  requirements REAL, NUMERALS, SUBSET, BOOLE, ARITHM;

begin

:: Mizar's n! is the source factorial.  The source natural-type filter is
:: extensionally the identity, and the factorial body is 1 at zero and
:: n!*(n+1) at successor n+1.  Splitting NAT into zero and successors unfolds
:: those two definitions without introducing any opaque auxiliary object.
:: Leibniz equality remains universal transport across predicates, represented
:: extensionally by subsets of NAT.

::$P-
theorem
  (for P being Subset of NAT st (0!) in P holds 1 in P) &
  (for n being Nat, P being Subset of NAT st ((n+1)!) in P
   holds (n!) * (n+1) in P)
proof
end;
::$P+
